WEBVTT

00:20.911 --> 00:24.501
OCTOBER 1013 AD
LONDON, ENGLAND

00:29.501 --> 00:31.591
THE BATTLE OF LONDON BRIDGE

00:40.641 --> 00:43.061
That's not really a bridge.

00:43.141 --> 00:44.981
It's more like a fortress.

00:45.061 --> 00:47.151
I'm impressed, London.

00:47.231 --> 00:49.901
The city has survived many attacks
over the years.

00:49.981 --> 00:51.821
It has a lot of history.

00:51.901 --> 00:55.911
This isn't the time to be complacent, Askeladd.

00:55.991 --> 00:57.911
This city's going to be trouble.

00:57.991 --> 01:00.831
You said it'd be an easy win.
That's why I'm here.

01:00.911 --> 01:03.001
Sorry, sorry.

01:03.081 --> 01:07.251
I never imagined
that Thorkell would side with the enemy.

01:11.301 --> 01:13.711
You mean, Thorkell the Tall?

01:13.801 --> 01:16.221
He's in bed with the enemy for the money.

01:16.301 --> 01:17.381
What a traitor.

01:19.261 --> 01:22.011
We're in this for the money too.

01:22.101 --> 01:26.231
We sided with the Army of Denmark,
because we thought King Sweyn has a chance to win.

01:30.611 --> 01:32.821
The other clans are all the same.

01:32.901 --> 01:36.151
They're desperate
to prove themselves on the battlefield

01:36.241 --> 01:39.321
and increase their share of the spoils.

01:39.411 --> 01:43.331
Well, with so many men here,
no one's getting very much.

01:45.121 --> 01:47.671
I don't fight for money.

01:47.751 --> 01:49.331
I like to kill.

01:51.251 --> 01:53.341
I can truly rely on a man like you, Bjorn.

01:53.421 --> 01:58.841
In any case, those bigwigs all want London.

01:59.511 --> 02:01.721
If we can capture the Thames River,

02:01.801 --> 02:04.721
we can set up a supply line
to the inland areas in Wessex.

02:06.641 --> 02:09.231
The top leaders all have their eyes
on this battleground.

02:09.311 --> 02:13.021
Yeah. This is the place to be if you want to stand out.

02:14.071 --> 02:15.611
What do you mean?

02:15.691 --> 02:18.031
Do you have a plan in mind?

02:18.111 --> 02:19.491
Well,

02:19.571 --> 02:21.991
it's not really a plan.

02:22.531 --> 02:23.531
Thorfinn.

02:25.081 --> 02:27.501
We have some work for you.

02:27.581 --> 02:29.371
Go bring me Thorkell's head.

02:35.131 --> 02:37.381
Promise me you'll give me my reward.

02:37.461 --> 02:39.551
Okay. Okay.

02:39.631 --> 02:42.511
The same as always, right?
You're so stubborn.

02:43.051 --> 02:45.351
Getting so worked up about a fight you can't win.

02:45.431 --> 02:48.101
Maybe you get it from your father.

02:52.351 --> 02:54.521
Don't forget, Askeladd.

02:54.611 --> 02:56.231
My only wish as a warrior

02:56.321 --> 02:59.701
is to beat you in a duel.

02:59.781 --> 03:03.161
Our next duel will be your last.

03:03.241 --> 03:05.241
I'm going to carve out your heart,

03:05.331 --> 03:07.831
and offer it to my father's spirit.

03:12.211 --> 03:13.961
Then get to work.

03:14.041 --> 03:17.591
Only those who fight
on the battlefield get what they desire.

03:17.671 --> 03:20.221
That's the way of the warrior.

03:24.471 --> 03:27.101
My head's not cheap, you know.

03:27.181 --> 03:30.851
I'll duel you as often as you like.

03:32.231 --> 03:35.231
Go bring me Thorkell's head.

05:10.831 --> 05:12.491
Hey.

05:12.581 --> 05:14.501
Askeladd.

05:15.081 --> 05:16.081
What?

05:16.171 --> 05:18.881
One ship is heading towards the bridge.

05:19.541 --> 05:23.131
It's the Jomsvikings! The Sea Deer!

05:23.711 --> 05:26.181
They're messengers from the regular army.

05:26.261 --> 05:27.511
Are they Floki's men?

05:28.681 --> 05:32.011
I bet he's going to try to win Thorkell over to his side

05:32.101 --> 05:35.391
by saying he'll pay double whatever England pays.

05:35.481 --> 05:37.351
Thorkell will follow the money.

05:37.441 --> 05:38.771
I bet he'll take their offer.

05:40.691 --> 05:43.401
Well, I'm not so sure about that.

05:45.031 --> 05:46.201
They're here.

05:46.281 --> 05:47.401
It's just one ship.

05:52.491 --> 05:54.411
This way. Hurry.

05:56.001 --> 05:58.171
Die. Take that.

05:58.251 --> 05:59.881
Take that.

05:59.961 --> 06:00.791
Fire. Fire.

06:01.381 --> 06:03.841
Don't shoot. We're messengers.

06:03.921 --> 06:06.171
We want to talk to Thorkell.

06:08.471 --> 06:09.931
-You damn bastards.
-Die.

06:10.551 --> 06:12.601
We didn't come here to fight.

06:12.681 --> 06:15.061
Where is Thorkell?

06:15.141 --> 06:18.231
Shut up. Die.

06:18.311 --> 06:20.061
Hey.

06:20.151 --> 06:21.771
Stop.

06:21.861 --> 06:22.821
Yes, sir.

06:22.901 --> 06:25.691
Everyone. Cease fire.

06:28.901 --> 06:33.331
Hey, Floki. It's been a while.

06:33.411 --> 06:36.081
You look like you've been doing well.

06:36.161 --> 06:38.461
Enough with the pleasantries.

06:38.541 --> 06:43.591
His Highness, King Sweyn, sends a message,
which I am here to deliver.

06:43.671 --> 06:45.841
In the words of His Highness:

06:46.881 --> 06:50.511
"The King of England has escaped
to the land of the Franks.

06:50.591 --> 06:53.101
Resistance is futile.

06:53.891 --> 06:55.641
Surrender.

06:55.721 --> 06:57.931
If you surrender, then in the name of Thor,

06:58.021 --> 07:00.641
I shall spare the lives of you and your men,

07:00.731 --> 07:03.111
as well as leave you your fortunes."

07:04.151 --> 07:07.151
Go back to the army, Thorkell.

07:07.231 --> 07:09.701
Those are the wishes of His Highness.

07:10.361 --> 07:12.781
Is King Sweyn here?

07:12.871 --> 07:14.241
He's tough.

07:14.321 --> 07:16.201
For such an old man.

07:16.291 --> 07:17.791
Thorkell.

07:17.871 --> 07:22.331
Why are you drawing your bow against a friend?

07:22.421 --> 07:27.461
For so long, we've fought as warriors, side by side.

07:28.511 --> 07:32.011
You must not misread the flow of the world.

07:32.091 --> 07:35.891
Your brother Sigvaldi is also worried.

07:37.351 --> 07:39.731
Flow of the world?

07:39.811 --> 07:41.391
I see.

07:41.481 --> 07:46.571
I was fighting against the English myself until last year.
That's why I know.

07:46.651 --> 07:49.151
They're really weak.

07:49.231 --> 07:52.361
-They're a bunch of sheltered city boys.
-What?

07:52.451 --> 07:53.911
-Is that Norse?
-They lack spirit.

07:53.991 --> 07:54.911
Maybe.

07:55.531 --> 07:59.081
Prince Edmund was the only general

07:59.161 --> 08:01.911
who could handle the army of Denmark.

08:02.001 --> 08:04.291
This country is finished.

08:04.371 --> 08:05.791
Oh, in that case...

08:05.881 --> 08:08.551
In other words,

08:09.251 --> 08:12.221
it'd be more fun

08:12.301 --> 08:14.931
to fight against you.

08:15.011 --> 08:16.431
What?

08:16.511 --> 08:18.511
That's enough talk.

08:18.601 --> 08:21.271
Let's get to the next part. The next part.

08:21.351 --> 08:23.561
Wait. Thorkell.

08:23.641 --> 08:28.111
I promise you double what England's giving you.

08:35.031 --> 08:38.451
Here I go, Floki.

08:38.531 --> 08:41.661
Veer left. Full speed.

08:42.251 --> 08:43.751
Time for the deadly...

08:43.831 --> 08:45.671
Keel-Buster!!

08:50.751 --> 08:53.421
Oh, I missed.

08:53.511 --> 08:54.551
Full speed.

08:54.631 --> 08:55.681
Withdraw.

08:58.261 --> 08:59.761
Men. Kill them.

08:59.851 --> 09:00.681
Yes, sir.

09:01.771 --> 09:04.021
Retreat. Retreat.

09:07.901 --> 09:10.191
Hey, Floki.

09:11.071 --> 09:13.651
Go ask King Sweyn

09:13.741 --> 09:18.161
whether he's bored
of always fighting battles he's going to win.

09:26.541 --> 09:29.381
There's no chance that we'll be able to convince him.

09:30.381 --> 09:31.841
I see.

09:31.921 --> 09:33.381
It was a waste of time.

09:33.461 --> 09:36.131
So, what shall we do?

09:41.971 --> 09:43.811
Attack them now, without delay.

10:02.371 --> 10:04.041
Hey. Damn.

10:16.471 --> 10:17.591
All right.

10:20.141 --> 10:22.721
Damn. They're attacking the pier.

10:24.221 --> 10:25.271
You bastard.

10:26.311 --> 10:27.601
Hurry.

10:27.681 --> 10:28.521
Damn.

10:28.601 --> 10:31.771
-Damn. I missed.
-Get more rocks.

10:31.861 --> 10:33.901
Out of my way.

10:33.981 --> 10:35.531
Wow.

10:35.611 --> 10:37.281
Here we go.

10:43.741 --> 10:46.451
How'd you like that?
That was my special...

10:46.541 --> 10:48.041
er... Log-Dropper!!

10:48.121 --> 10:49.371
The name says it all.

10:49.461 --> 10:50.501
That was amazing.

10:50.581 --> 10:51.751
Next.

10:51.831 --> 10:52.881
Hurry up.

10:52.961 --> 10:53.841
Yes, sir.

10:59.511 --> 11:02.011
What's wrong with Sweyn's army?

11:02.091 --> 11:04.301
Why don't you come up with something?

11:04.391 --> 11:07.471
I know you can do better if you try.

11:07.561 --> 11:12.731
At this rate, you won't capture London Bridge.
Not even in a hundred years...

11:24.201 --> 11:27.491
This is it. This guy looks fun.

11:27.581 --> 11:29.911
Thorfinn. Can you hear me?

11:30.001 --> 11:33.041
The huge man in front with the log.

11:33.131 --> 11:34.381
That's Thorkell.

11:35.461 --> 11:37.591
This is no good. Stop the ship.

11:37.671 --> 11:39.511
He'll hit us if we get any closer.

11:39.591 --> 11:41.221
Steer left.

11:41.301 --> 11:42.631
Just a little further.

11:45.221 --> 11:47.221
All right. That's enough.

11:47.311 --> 11:48.721
Jump.

11:49.431 --> 11:51.601
Don't touch him.

11:51.691 --> 11:54.101
This jolly little fool...

11:55.111 --> 11:57.901
is all mine.

11:58.821 --> 11:59.941
Yeah.

12:02.241 --> 12:03.361
Bastard.

12:06.581 --> 12:07.621
Come on.

12:17.541 --> 12:18.591
You're good...

12:19.631 --> 12:20.961
For a kid.

12:29.011 --> 12:31.311
Don't touch him.

12:32.021 --> 12:35.601
I'll answer the challenge of this suicide attacker.

12:38.021 --> 12:39.441
It's one-on-one.

12:43.991 --> 12:47.571
All right. Bring it on, kid.

12:48.331 --> 12:50.081
One-on-one, and unarmed?

12:50.661 --> 12:52.041
Don't underestimate me.

13:03.631 --> 13:06.261
Oh, he was aiming for my wrist.

13:06.341 --> 13:08.391
Good job, kid.

13:12.221 --> 13:14.311
I can see why he's so confident.

13:14.391 --> 13:16.651
With a body and fists as big as his,

13:16.731 --> 13:18.651
I'd be dead with one hit.

13:19.271 --> 13:20.981
I like you.

13:21.071 --> 13:23.531
I'm going to have some fun.

13:24.071 --> 13:24.901
What?

13:27.491 --> 13:28.871
Take that.

13:31.201 --> 13:32.291
Oops.

13:32.951 --> 13:33.791
Damn.

13:35.911 --> 13:37.671
That was close.

13:40.131 --> 13:41.041
I can't reach him.

13:42.341 --> 13:45.011
All his weak points are up high.

13:45.091 --> 13:46.721
Below his armpit.

13:46.801 --> 13:47.801
His neck.

13:47.881 --> 13:48.931
All right.

13:54.851 --> 13:55.981
He's low.

13:56.771 --> 13:58.231
So...

13:58.311 --> 13:59.481
I'll kick him.

13:59.561 --> 14:00.771
Run in there.

14:17.121 --> 14:18.961
That hurts.

14:19.041 --> 14:21.541
But I got you.

14:27.221 --> 14:28.551
You did it.

14:28.631 --> 14:29.881
Great, captain.

14:29.971 --> 14:30.801
Kill him.

14:30.891 --> 14:32.851
It's not over yet.

14:32.931 --> 14:35.181
Here we go.

14:37.521 --> 14:39.191
Oh, dear.

14:39.271 --> 14:40.731
This won't work.

14:40.811 --> 14:42.941
Thorfinn's getting beaten to a pulp.

14:43.611 --> 14:45.281
I guess it wasn't going to work.

14:45.361 --> 14:46.441
Yeah.

14:48.531 --> 14:49.701
Askeladd.

14:49.781 --> 14:51.111
That's the signal.

14:51.201 --> 14:53.371
Yeah. Then it's time to retreat.

14:54.661 --> 14:56.451
Retreat.

14:56.541 --> 14:58.331
Withdraw all units.

15:00.961 --> 15:02.921
What? No.

15:03.001 --> 15:06.501
The battle ended while I was playing with the kid.

15:06.591 --> 15:07.671
Hey, kid.

15:07.761 --> 15:09.591
It looks like they abandoned you.

15:09.671 --> 15:11.091
Poor kid.

15:11.181 --> 15:13.601
Even though you tried hard.

15:14.931 --> 15:16.601
What? Is he dead?

15:16.681 --> 15:17.771
Hey.

15:17.851 --> 15:19.231
Hey. Hey. Hey.

15:41.331 --> 15:44.001
You still haven't lost the will to fight?

15:44.081 --> 15:46.711
You're good, even though you're small.

15:51.631 --> 15:53.181
Warrior.

15:53.261 --> 15:55.051
Tell me your name.

16:01.351 --> 16:02.351
Thorfinn.

16:04.061 --> 16:05.521
Son of Thors.

16:05.611 --> 16:06.731
I'm Thorfinn.

16:07.821 --> 16:09.191
Thors?

16:09.281 --> 16:11.491
Hey. Thors? Do you mean...?

16:15.201 --> 16:17.121
Oh, there he goes.

16:19.701 --> 16:21.331
Captain, your orders?

16:21.411 --> 16:22.541
Shall we shoot him?

16:23.961 --> 16:25.541
Don't shoot.

16:25.631 --> 16:27.131
We'll let him go today.

16:28.881 --> 16:30.131
Hey.

16:30.211 --> 16:32.921
Warrior Thorfinn.

16:33.011 --> 16:35.051
That was fun.

16:35.141 --> 16:36.851
Let's do this again.

16:37.551 --> 16:40.561
Let's finish things off next time.

16:40.641 --> 16:43.101
Promise me.

16:53.781 --> 16:55.741
That hurts.

16:55.821 --> 16:56.781
Kill me, please.

16:56.871 --> 16:59.201
Does anyone want to be killed?

16:59.281 --> 17:01.241
I can kill you.

17:04.911 --> 17:06.501
He's not going to make it.

17:07.171 --> 17:09.001
He's been stabbed in the gut.

17:09.091 --> 17:10.301
We can't save him.

17:10.381 --> 17:13.421
Hey. Bring some onion soup over here.

17:13.511 --> 17:14.591
Torgrim.

17:14.671 --> 17:15.761
Take care of this.

17:22.271 --> 17:23.851
I see.

17:23.931 --> 17:25.771
So, we can't capture London.

17:26.521 --> 17:27.441
No.

17:27.521 --> 17:29.771
It's not that we can't capture London.

17:29.861 --> 17:32.401
It will just take some time.

17:33.111 --> 17:36.031
Time? How much time, Floki?

17:36.111 --> 17:39.531
Yes. It depends on the size of their stockpile.

17:40.581 --> 17:41.871
One year.

17:41.951 --> 17:45.041
No. A half-year, if things go well.

17:45.121 --> 17:47.121
It's already autumn.

17:47.211 --> 17:50.541
We cannot spend so much time on just one city.

17:52.631 --> 17:55.511
The overall situation is most important.

17:55.591 --> 17:57.131
In everything we do,

17:57.221 --> 18:01.431
we must prioritize gaining control over all of England.

18:01.511 --> 18:02.351
Yes, sir.

18:03.391 --> 18:05.891
We shall move our main forces to the west.

18:05.981 --> 18:07.641
Leave 4000 soldiers

18:07.731 --> 18:10.901
to continue the siege on London.

18:10.981 --> 18:12.691
As you wish.

18:16.281 --> 18:20.451
The 4000 soldiers will be under the command of...

18:23.991 --> 18:26.501
Canute.

18:27.331 --> 18:30.121
This is a good chance to boost his standing.

18:30.211 --> 18:31.211
What?

18:32.461 --> 18:34.501
That's not what we agreed upon.

18:34.591 --> 18:38.261
The reason His Highness came
to serve as a good example for the people.

18:38.341 --> 18:39.631
That's what you said.

18:39.721 --> 18:42.391
Ragnar. Please, refrain.

18:42.471 --> 18:44.141
This is His Highness's will.

18:44.221 --> 18:47.891
Against Thorkell,
even the entire army stands no chance.

18:47.981 --> 18:50.351
To defeat him with only one-fifth of the forces...

18:50.441 --> 18:51.271
It's impossible.

18:51.981 --> 18:55.021
Having so few men is the only way to help him.

18:55.111 --> 18:56.151
But...

18:56.231 --> 19:00.071
His Highness is unfamiliar with battle,
and is experiencing emotional distress.

19:00.151 --> 19:03.831
This is your responsibility, Ragnar.

19:05.411 --> 19:08.001
Maybe it's because of the teachings of Christ.

19:08.081 --> 19:12.631
He grew up to be faint of heart,
even though he's a man.

19:12.711 --> 19:15.341
It's because you spoiled him.

19:17.711 --> 19:19.511
I apologize.

19:20.551 --> 19:24.301
To Canute,
I shall leave the soldiers laying siege to London.

19:24.391 --> 19:28.221
You shall accompany him,
and provide support, as his assistant.

19:40.611 --> 19:41.611
Your Highness...

20:23.241 --> 20:25.451
My shoulder is dislocated.

20:25.531 --> 20:28.161
And my right ankle is sprained.

20:28.241 --> 20:30.451
And I have a few broken ribs.

20:32.541 --> 20:33.581
Damn it.

20:33.671 --> 20:35.381
That madman.

20:38.001 --> 20:39.381
Hey. Can you see them?

20:42.761 --> 20:45.511
Most of them have retreated.

20:45.591 --> 20:46.431
What?

20:46.511 --> 20:48.891
Does that mean...?

20:48.971 --> 20:50.011
Did we...

20:50.101 --> 20:51.181
win?

20:52.391 --> 20:53.601
We won?

20:53.691 --> 20:57.731
-They ran away with their tails between their legs?
-Then we have won.

20:58.771 --> 21:00.531
What?

21:00.611 --> 21:02.531
What's going on?

21:02.611 --> 21:04.651
We did it. We won.

21:04.741 --> 21:05.571
What?

21:05.661 --> 21:07.371
We won.

21:07.451 --> 21:09.081
Hey, hey.

21:09.161 --> 21:10.541
Hey.

21:10.621 --> 21:12.831
Let's fight some more.

21:12.911 --> 21:15.081
Hey. Hold on.

21:15.161 --> 21:16.211
Hey.

21:19.211 --> 21:21.591
You idiots.

21:22.261 --> 21:25.131
Are you giving up on London?

21:25.221 --> 21:28.091
Come back, you cowards.

21:28.181 --> 21:31.011
Fight me.

21:36.061 --> 21:39.151
Oh, what a pain.

21:39.231 --> 21:41.111
Thorkell, you bastard.

21:44.781 --> 21:47.491
Hey. What happened? You're alive?

21:47.571 --> 21:50.491
You look terrible.

21:51.581 --> 21:55.001
You had a bad opponent, Thorfinn.

21:58.331 --> 22:02.381
By the way, I'm going to march on Wessex.
What about you?

22:02.461 --> 22:05.381
If it hurts to walk, I'll just leave you here.

22:27.401 --> 22:29.571
We're going to get rich in Wessex.

22:29.661 --> 22:31.661
I can't wait.

22:31.741 --> 22:34.951
-You only got one arm.
-I can handle anyone.

22:35.041 --> 22:36.621
I'll kill them all.

22:51.591 --> 22:54.101
That was fun.

22:54.181 --> 22:56.181
Let's do this again.

23:00.981 --> 23:02.811
That madman.

23:05.531 --> 23:09.861
What's so enjoyable about battle?
